    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51046.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 2,
    "turn_text": "Well, they're all both sides are on their listening tours and they're out, you know, taking testimony or taking comments from the public. But, you know, until the election's over, we're not going to know where this thing is going. You know, because of the Republicans take over the House and Senate, it's a very different situation than if the Democrats control the House and Senate. So the first thing you've got to do is figure out who's going to be in charge. The one thing we know is the President's going to be there, you know, and the one thing I keep cautioning people about is not getting down this rabbit hole on food stamps, because if the Democrats aren't happy, you know, which they happened the last two farm bills and they failed in the house, if they're not happy, Biden will veto the bill, even if they get one done.",
