    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51046.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "Well, you know, this is a worldwide issue. It's not just the United States. You know, the Biden administration cut back a little bit on, you know, some of the drilling and public lands and offshore and so forth. I'm not sure that had that big of an impact. I think it's more of a A worldwide phenomena, the war in Ukraine and so forth. Apparently in the United States we don't have enough refining capacity. So it's not a matter of not having enough oil so we don't have enough refining capacity. And that's because people oppose refineries. Some people out there trying to push electric cars. get rid of the oil industry and all that stuff didn't help anything. So the truth is, in my opinion, we need all the energy sources we can get. Whether it's oil, gas, coal, electric, solar, wind, whatever it is, we need it all. And we've got people out there that say, well, I just want to have this and I want to have that and that's the problem.",
