  {
    "episode_id": 51046,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51046.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "Well, it's, you know, I don't have to get on plane every day and go to DC, which is a big plus. And I've only been there three times since the election. And I try to avoid it, if I can. But I've been working with some of the groups, you know, that I've worked with when I was in the Congress. And so I'm actually probably busier now than I was. when I was in Congress, you know, but I don't have to run all over the world, you know, like I did back then. And I've got my son working with me who, he was my financial guy through our campaigns and so forth, and he wanted to change occupations. He's been going to DC for the last year about, you know, getting to know people going very well and people like him. And, you know, he goes into an office and he says, I'm Elliott Peterson and I'm Collins. Collins, my dad. And they said, oh, God, we love your dad. Come on in. You know, so I made it's like it gives him access to, you know, both sides of the aisle, frankly. And so we've been, you know, working for some people in some of these issues. We're also set up this Midwest Council that we're Hoping to have a big impact on the next farm bill, you know, kind of advocating for things that are going to be important for the Midwest. And we're in the process of, you know, August, we're going to have a kind of our first policy center meeting. We're trying to bring the universities into this. to have them help us figure out these are economists. So it's not the normal thing that you work with with the university. These are the economists from the different universities to help us figure out how much something costs, you know, what can make sense in the Midwest and so forth. Texas and Mississippi have been doing this very effectively. And we haven't, you know, we've kind of been working state by state and crop by crop. And, you know, if you're going to get anything done in this climate, you're going to have to work together. And so we're putting that together. And so I'm busy, you know, I'm down here today and putting a few miles on the plane here and there. Good",
